1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Welcome back. Today we're looking at
how light bends when it changes material.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,000
This is called <i>refraction</i>.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,500
光从空气进入水中时，
速度会变慢。

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,500
That's why a straw looks broken
in a glass of water.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
这就是为什么吸管看起来像是<b>折断</b>了。

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,800
The amount of bending depends on the
refractive index of each material.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
折射率越大，光在其中传播得越慢。

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
Let's try a quick example with glass.

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,600
Glass has a refractive index of about 1.5,
so light travels at two-thirds of its speed in air.

10
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:43,000
玻璃的折射率大约是一点五。

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,900
Now watch what happens at a steep angle.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,200
<i>Total internal reflection.</i>
全反射。

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,500
This is exactly how optical fibres
carry light around corners.

14
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,000
光纤就是利用这个原理传输信号的。

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,500
So, three things to remember.

16
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,800
Light slows down in denser materials,
it bends towards the normal,

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,500
and past the critical angle, it reflects completely.

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
谢谢观看，我们下次见！
